{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmtGPQ32gUCgQVKNvhG8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B4bBhn6CTt9R2vdGrwEqxr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-838\\docs\\reviews\\wi-838-first-mint-takes-a-lease\\002-ADJUDICATE-6fd4e8b.md","content":"# WI-838 — adjudication 002 (meaning vs clarity), at 6fd4e8b\n\nAnchor: `docs/archive/last_approved/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml`\n(copied 2026-10-06, f9265d99). Judged: LLR-270 `Detail`, the one amended cell shown.\nThis sitting judges again the row that adjudication 001 returned.\n\n- [MEANING] LLR-270 Detail -> before: keep_for takes the lease on an existing record and waits up to lease_wait on any lease another call holds, then runs unretained saying why; keep_bookkeep and keep_abandon release it; a route with NO record mints with no lease held before launch; a retired or absent record mints; a raising launch's keep_abandon retires the resumed session, and a tombstone always names a session to retire -> after: the same general wait (now \"while another call holds the route's lease\") and release (\"keep_bookkeep and keep_abandon release the lease\") are kept, PLUS: where no record exists keep_for writes a lease-only record {family, route_id, lease} under the store lock BEFORE launch; a lease-only record mints and only an active or draining record resumes; a crashed first call's lease-only record is retired by the expired-lease rule; a mint lands only while the route record still carries its own lease, else it lands on nothing with reset reason `store moved on` whether the taker still runs or has finished; a first mint that raises removes its lease-only record, and so does a tombstone after dropping the holder's lease -> not the same: code built correctly to the old text (a first mint holds nothing, so two first calls both mint and the later bookkeeping replaces the earlier session's record) fails the new text (lease-only record before launch, the second call waits then runs unretained, `store moved on`). The added obligations are sound and match WI-838's Done-when. Adjudication 001's finding (the general lease wait and release had been dropped) is answered: both are stated again with their old scope. I would bless this text, and re-attest it on the released LLR rung.\n\nVERDICT: MEANING rows=1\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":352,"cache_read_input_tokens":75774,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":352},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2584b99b-5c67-48ab-94cc-44374d289363","uuid":"8751a62b-0333-4496-af79-85911fcc5740","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:53:59.044Z","request_id":"req_011CfmtGP7B9fME6X5orywGv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01B4bBhn6CTt9R2vdGrwEqxr":{"file_path":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-838\\docs\\reviews\\wi-838-first-mint-takes-a-lease\\002-ADJUDICATE-6fd4e8b.md","content":"# WI-838 — adjudication 002 (meaning vs clarity), at 6fd4e8b\n\nAnchor: `docs/archive/last_approved/docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml`\n(copied 2026-10-06, f9265d99). Judged: LLR-270 `Detail`, the one amended cell shown.\nThis sitting judges again the row that adjudication 001 returned.\n\n- [MEANING] LLR-270 Detail -> before: keep_for takes the lease on an existin
[... byte cap hit — full stream in out/run-logs/ ...]
uals a fresh session's, and keep_warmer builds no warmer. For a covered call, plan_keep asks LLR-305's sign-in refusal before keep_for, so a refusal takes no lease and creates no home. STORE. primary_out_dir resolves the primary checkout's out/ directory from the git common directory; store_dir places one JSON record per route (IF-247) in its adjudicator child, so it outlives a lane worktree. dir_lock is the shared exclusive-file locking primitive for a named runtime-store directory; store_lock applies it to the adjudicator store. Every retained-session read-modify-write holds store_lock, a file created exclusively and stale after two minutes; each record is written through its own mkstemp file and os.replace. A record carries a lease {holder, until}: keep_for takes it for the adjudication's wall deadline plus 300 s, waits up to lease_wait seconds while another call holds it, and past that runs the adjudication unretained, saying why; keep_bookkeep and keep_abandon release it. A lease that EXPIRED without being released means its holder is still running past it or crashed, so the session is never reused: keep_for (and take_warm_lease) retires it with reason lease expired unreleased and drops the stale lease (retire_stale_lease), and the launch mints fresh. BEFORE A LAUNCH (keep_for, under the lock): a retired or absent record mints; with reset_on_same_artifact, a session that judged this work item retires; drain_reason drains an active session whose governing_hash changed (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md, docs/process.toml, every .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md and .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md, and the template of every brief class the dial's retain_for names, each as its override text when one is wired, else its shipped file) or whose runner version (cli_version, the runner's --version, read by plan_keep) differs from the one it was minted under; a draining session retires at a clear point, is_clear_point over the work-item rows: the work item being launched does not continue a chain the session judged, and chain_pending finds no queued adjudication and no active row in such a chain; otherwise it is resumed. A work item belongs to such a chain when its lineage, the transitive closure of its Predecessors and Supersedes links through the registry (a cycle ending where it closes), holds an item the session judged, so a re-adjudication naming only the worker an adjudication sent back is in that adjudication's chain. LAUNCH (act): keep_argv gives the adapter's resume form (claude --resume <id>, codex exec resume <id> without -C or --ephemeral, opencode --session <id>) or mint form (claude --session-id <uuid4>; codex and opencode report their id in their JSON stream), under the family's dedicated home (HOME_VARIABLES: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, CODEX_HOME) created under the store's home/ and merged over the call's environment; opencode keeps its shared home. AFTER (keep_bookkeep, under the lock): the call's session id, occupancy, window and percent are folded into the record, the work item appended to judged; a non-zero exit, a timeout or a reported is_error retires the session at once, and an occupancy percent at the dial (codex clamped to 85, FAMILY_RESET_CAP) drains it; a record another session replaced meanwhile is left alone; the call's accounting gains session-gen and reset-reason. A launch that raises retires the session it resumed (keep_abandon), guaranteed under lock contention: a tombstone (<record>.retire, written whole with no lock) naming the session, the reason and the lease holder is written first and applied at once if the lock can be had within a second; every locked read of the record (load_honoured, in keep_for, keep_bookkeep and take_warm_lease) applies a pending tombstone before anything else, retiring that session and dropping its holder's lease, and the lockless keep-warm read skips a marked record. KEEP-WARM (KeepWarmer, built by keep_warmer when keepwarm_minutes is also on, ticked once per dispatcher poll by run): keepwarm_due is true for an ANTHROPIC active session idle keepwarm_minutes while lanes are out, and a ping is taken only on a route whose runner's adapter bounds a call to one turn (claude's), so a route served through any other runner is never pinged; take_warm_lease takes its lease under the lock, or names why not (leased to another call, the lock held); the ping (role KEEP-WARM, source keep-warm, prompt ack, bounded by one_turn to --max-turns 1, a 300 s wall) runs on its own thread through act, so the tick never waits; one ping at a time, a due ping while one is in flight skipped and said; its session log is written and committed by the dispatcher's own thread between polls and only over a clean trunk, else held and said; at the run's end a ping in flight is waited out and recorded by the same rule, over a clean trunk only, and over a dirty one its log is not written and the reason is printed and returned.\"\"\"","+code_symbol = \"KeepConfig/keep_config/applies/FAMILY_RESET_CAP/GOVERNING_INPUT_FILES/GOVERNING_INPUT_GLOBS/HOME_VARIABLES/primary_out_dir/store_lock/dir_lock/store_load/write_tombstone/load_honoured/is_lease_only/_apply_tombstone/store_remove/retire_stale_lease/dedicated_home_env/governing_hash/drain_reason/lineage/chain_pending/is_clear_point/keep_for/keep_argv/keep_bookkeep/keep_abandon/keepwarm_due/take_warm_lease;cli_version/plan_keep/KeepWarmer/keep_warmer;ClaudeAdapter.mint/ClaudeAdapter.resume/ClaudeAdapter.one_turn/PlainAdapter.bounds_one_turn/CodexAdapter.resume/OpencodeAdapter.resume/reported_error;adjudication_keep;run\"","+ detail = \"\"\"CONFIG. keep_config reads [adjudicator] (context_reset_pct 0..100, retain_for, keepwarm_minutes, reset_on_same_artifact); a missing table or an out-of-type value reads as that field's default. applies is true only for an ADJUDICATE call of a retain_for brief on a named route with context_reset_pct above 0; otherwise plan_keep returns None before reading the runner version or the store, so at dial 0 nothing is minted, no resume flag is added, no store is written, the launch equals a fresh session's, and keep_warmer builds no warmer. For a covered call, plan_keep asks LLR-305's sign-in refusal before keep_for, so a refusal takes no lease and creates no home. STORE. primary_out_dir resolves the primary checkout's out/ directory from the git common directory; store_dir places one JSON record per route (IF-247) in its adjudicator child, so it outlives a lane worktree. dir_lock is the shared exclusive-file locking primitive for a named runtime-store directory; store_lock applies it to the adjudicator store. Every retained-session read-modify-write holds store_lock, a file created exclusively and stale after two minutes; each record is written through its own mkstemp file and os.replace. A record carries a lease {holder, until}: keep_for takes it for the adjudication's wall deadline plus 300 s and, while another call holds the route's lease, waits up to lease_wait seconds before running the adjudication unretained and saying why. keep_bookkeep and keep_abandon release the lease. Where no record exists, keep_for writes a lease-only record holding family, route_id and the lease under the store lock before launch, so a first mint holds the route; keep_bookkeep completes the lease-only record, and keep_abandon removes it when that first mint raises. A lease that EXPIRED without being released means its holder is still running past it or crashed, so the session is never reused: keep_for (and take_warm_lease) retires it with reason lease expired unreleased and drops the stale lease (retire_stale_lease), and the launch mints fresh. This also retires a crashed first call's lease-only record, which remains without a session id. BEFORE A LAUNCH (keep_for, under the lock): a retired, absent or lease-only record mints; only an active or draining record resumes; with reset_on_same_artifact, a session that judged this work item retires; drain_reason drains an active session whose governing_hash changed (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, GEMINI.md, docs/process.toml, every .claude/skills/*/SKILL.md and .agents/skills/*/SKILL.md, and the template of every brief class the dial's retain_for names, each as its override text when one is wired, else its shipped file) or whose runner version (cli_version, the runner's --version, read by plan_keep) differs from the one it was minted under; a draining session retires at a clear point, is_clear_point over the work-item rows: the work item being launched does not continue a chain the session judged, and chain_pending finds no queued adjudication and no active row in such a chain; otherwise it is resumed. A work item belongs to such a chain when its lineage, the transitive closure of its Predecessors and Supersedes links through the registry (a cycle ending where it closes), holds an item the session judged, so a re-adjudication naming only the worker an adjudication sent back is in that adjudication's chain. LAUNCH (act): keep_argv gives the adapter's resume form (claude --resume <id>, codex exec resume <id> without -C or --ephemeral, opencode --session <id>) or mint form (claude --session-id <uuid4>; codex and opencode report their id in their JSON stream), under the family's dedicated home (HOME_VARIABLES: CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR, CODEX_HOME) created under the store's home/ and merged over the call's environment; opencode keeps its shared home. AFTER (keep_bookkeep, under the lock): the call's session id, occupancy, window and percent are folded into the record, the work item appended to judged; a non-zero exit, a timeout or a reported is_error retires the session at once, and an occupancy percent at the dial (codex clamped to 85, FAMILY_RESET_CAP) drains it; a record another session replaced meanwhile is left alone; a mint lands only while the route record still carries its own lease; when another call took that lease over, the mint lands on nothing with reset reason store moved on whether that call still runs or has finished; the call's accounting gains session-gen and reset-reason. A launch that raises retires the session it resumed (keep_abandon); a first mint that raises removes its lease-only record. This is guaranteed under lock contention: a tombstone (<record>.retire, written whole with no lock) naming the session, the reason and the lease holder is written first and applied at once if the lock can be had within a second; every locked read of the record (load_honoured, in keep_for, keep_bookkeep and take_warm_lease) applies a pending tombstone before anything else, retiring that session and dropping its holder's lease, or removing a lease-only record after dropping its holder's lease, and the lockless keep-warm read skips a marked record. KEEP-WARM (KeepWarmer, built by keep_warmer when keepwarm_minutes is also on, ticked once per dispatcher poll by run): keepwarm_due is true for an ANTHROPIC active session idle keepwarm_minutes while lanes are out, and a ping is taken only on a route whose runner's adapter bounds a call to one turn (claude's), so a route served through any other runner is never pinged; take_warm_lease takes its lease under the lock, or names why not (leased to another call, the lock held); the ping (role KEEP-WARM, source keep-warm, prompt ack, bounded by one_turn to --max-turns 1, a 300 s wall) runs on its own thread through act, so the tick never waits; one ping at a time, a due ping while one is in flight skipped and said; its session log is written and committed by the dispatcher's own thread between polls and only over a clean trunk, else held and said; at the run's end a ping in flight is waited out and recorded by the same rule, over a clean trunk only, and over a dirty one its log is not written and the reason is printed and returned.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Retention is one more thing a call does, not a second launch path, so resume, occupancy, reset and keep-warm all go through act and record, and the rules and the store sit in their own module beside the service rather than in the roles. The layer ships off because turning it on is the owner's decision after it has been verified on the machine it runs on, and at the off dial the launch is exactly a fresh session's. The lock and the lease exist because a lane's worker and the dispatcher both reach the one store and the one transcript: a torn record or two calls resuming one session at once corrupts the state every later judgement reads. The clear point reads the queue and the lanes rather than the item alone because a draining session that retires while a successor of its own verdict is still queued breaks the round trip the layer exists for. The keep-warm ping is off the dispatcher's thread so a slow ping cannot stall the merges, and its record is on it so its commit is serialised with them. The dedicated homes keep a retained transcript out of a person's own sessions; credentials are provisioned into them by a person.\"\"\"","-test_refs = \"(see TC-266, TC-267, TC-268, TC-322)\"","+test_refs = \"(see TC-266, TC-267, TC-268, TC-322, TC-329)\""," status = \"Approved\""," component = \"CMP-008\""," phase = 6"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-838\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-838\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-838\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\low-level-requirements.toml"]}}}
