{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmtMT8QRqJibT9ePS4DV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: MEANING, 1 row (LLR-270 `Detail`). I approved the new text and re-attested it.**\n\n**Why it's MEANING:** Code built correctly to the old text would fail the new one. Under the old text, a route's first call took no lease, so two first calls could both mint and the later bookkeeping replaced the earlier session's record. The new text requires:\n- `keep_for` writes a lease-only record under the store lock before launching.\n- A second call that meets that lease waits, then runs without a retained session.\n- A mint is saved only if the record still holds its own lease. Otherwise it is dropped with reset reason `store moved on`.\n- A first mint that fails, or a tombstone, removes the lease-only record.\n\n**Why I approved it:** The finding from round 001 is fixed. The general wait (\"while another call holds the route's lease\") and the release (\"keep_bookkeep and keep_abandon release the lease\") are stated again with their old scope. The new first-mint rules are sound and match WI-838's Done-when.\n\n**Commits, each with the `WI: WI-838` trailer:**\n- `ad875969`: the verdict, at `docs/reviews/wi-838-first-mint-takes-a-lease/002-ADJUDICATE-6fd4e8b.md`.\n- `d5dee0cc`: the re-attestation, from `intake.py snapshot --reattests LLR-270`. The copy went through without a refusal and added act seq 42 with `reattested = [\"LLR-270\"]`.\n\n**Other notes:**\n- The snapshot command is at `project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py`; the `scripts/intake.py` path in the brief doesn't exist in this repo.\n- Round 001's `## Dispositions` section is gone from the WI-838 spec, replaced by an \"answered in this lane\" note, so no duplicate follow-up gets created at merge.\n- I changed no registry cells."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creat